## Outcomes / Summary
Reconciled a stale local `main` onto the real, already-merged GitHub state (PR #1), then added
genuinely new documentation (GOVERNANCE.md, MAINTAINERS.md, docs/ATTRIBUTION-AND-TRUST.md,
docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/FORMATS.md, docs/CLI.md, docs/UCI.md, docs/IDENTITY-PIECES.md,
docs/PROJECT-STORY.md, docs/GETTING-STARTED.md, docs/ROADMAP.md, docs/FAQ.md,
docs/FILE-HEADER-CONVENTION.md) without duplicating or contradicting what already existed.
Applied a per-file SPDX header + version convention across all 148 source files, fixed two real
pre-existing bugs and two factual doc errors, and used two background agents to close genuine
rustdoc/TSDoc density gaps. Full verification is green on both the Rust and TypeScript sides.
Repo deletion/recreation was explicitly reversed in favor of a normal PR, per user confirmation.
